{:id :EACL-FORMAL-071
 :status :fixed
 :discovered-by :manual-review
 :seed-or-trace
 "public-value/boolean-false-confused-with-absence"
 :minimized-fixture "fixture.edn"
 :impact :omission
 :affected-versions
 ["v8.0 pre-release before value-presence hardening"]
 :affected-backends
 [:shared :datomic :datahike :datalevin :datascript :third-party]
 :root-cause
 "Public validation admitted every non-nil identity and several request values, but later branches used host-language truthiness as a proxy for value presence. Boolean false was therefore a valid public identity at one boundary and an absent filter or cursor coordinate at another; explicit false execution controls were likewise defaulted or ignored."
 :fix
 "Use non-nil value presence for public IDs throughout filter resolution, cursor conversion, and backend identity resolution; reject explicit false evaluation, timeout, and cancellation controls with typed errors; cover the distinction in Dafny, portable mutation controls, and a real DataScript authorization/inspection/pagination regression."
 :closing-evidence
